### caco bd -- Bead (work item) management

Beads are the unit of work in Cacophony. Every task, bug, feature, and epic is
tracked as a bead.

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `caco bd show --bead-id <id>` | View full bead details (title, description, status, dependencies) |
| `caco bd list` | List beads (filter with `--status`, `--ready`, `--assignee`, `--type`, `--limit`) |
| `caco bd search --test-name <name>` | Search bead title/description text across all statuses for a test name |
| `caco bd create` | Create a new bead (`--title`, `--description`, `--type`, `--labels`, `--priority`, `--claim`) |
| `caco bd claim --bead-id <id>` | Claim an open bead for work |
| `caco bd update --bead-id <id>` | Update bead fields (status, priority, labels, title, description, dependencies) |
| `caco bd info --bead-id <id>` | Alias for show |
| `caco bd sync` | Force immediate sync of the bead database |
| `caco bd expand --text "..."` | Expand free-form text into structured beads via LLM |

**Bead statuses**: `open` (unstarted), `in_progress` (claimed, being worked),
`blocked` (waiting on dependencies), `closed` (finished), `draft` (not yet
actionable), `permanent` (ongoing reference).

**Bead types**: `task`, `bug`, `feature`, `epic`.


